SUMMARY:Deadline: School for Advanced Research: Native Artist Fellowships 2
 027 (USD 15\,000 plus Santa Fe residency)
DESCRIPTION:The Indian Arts Research Center at the School for Advanced Rese
 arch offers three residential fellowships for Native American artists: the
  Eric and Barbara Dobkin Fellowship for Native women artists working in an
 y media (including digital art and film/video)\, the Ronald and Susan Dubi
 n Fellowship for traditional arts\, and the Rollin and Mary Ella King Fell
 owship for Native visual artists from...\n\nOrganisation: School for Advan
 ced Research\, Indian Arts Research Center\nLocation: Santa Fe\, New Mexic
 o\, USA. RESTRICTED: Native American artists.\nAward: USD 15\,000 stipend 
 plus housing\, studio space\, a supplies allowance and travel. No applicat
 ion fee stated.\nDuration: Residency in Santa Fe (length varies by fellows
 hip)\n\nMore: https://sarweb.org/iarc/native-american-artist-fellowships/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sarweb.org/iarc/native-american-artist-fellowships/?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Santa Fe\, New Mexico\, USA. RESTRICTED: Native American artists.
END:VEVENT
