SUMMARY:Deadline: Bernheim Arboretum and Research Forest: Artist in Residen
 ce 2027 (Kentucky\, USD 2\,500 stipend)
DESCRIPTION:Annual residency in which artists live at Bernheim Arboretum an
 d Research Forest and create site-specific work inspired by total immersio
 n in the natural environment. WHO: visual and mixed-media artists\, includ
 ing those working with sound and with performance that incorporates visual
  elements.\n\nOrganisation: Bernheim Arboretum and Research Forest (Arts i
 n Nature programme)\nLocation: Bernheim Arboretum and Research Forest\, Cl
 ermont\, Kentucky\, USA (on-site cabin and studio)\nAward: USD 2\,500 stip
 end\, plus a furnished one-bedroom cabin (kitchen\, bath\, Wi-Fi)\, a stud
 io near a 32-acre lake\, staff support\, and free or discounted classes an
 d events. No application fee stated.\nDuration: 6-8 weeks recommended\, or
  two periods of at least 3 weeks each\, in 2027.\n\nMore: https://bernheim
 .org/news/call-for-2027-artist-in-residence/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://bernheim.org/news/call-for-2027-artist-in-residence/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Bernheim Arboretum and Research Forest\, Clermont\, Kentucky\, USA
  (on-site cabin and studio)
